 "result": "`routes_command` in `src/tessel/cli.py:1047-1106`, registered as the `routes` command on `TesselGroup`.\n\n**Sorting:**\n- `--sort/-s` takes one of `endpoint` (default), `methods`, `domain`, `rule` or `match`.\n- It builds rows of `[endpoint, methods, (host/subdomain if any rule has one), rule]` and sorts them with `rows.sort(key=itemgetter(sorts.index(sort)))`, so it sorts by the chosen column.\n- `domain` is only a valid column when some rule has a host or subdomain.\n- `match` isn't in the `sorts` list, so `index` raises `ValueError`, which is caught and ignored. The rows then stay in `url_map.iter_rules()` order, which is the order Tessel matches routes in.\n\n`HEAD` and `OPTIONS` are hidden unless `--all-methods` is passed.",
